 "honest_headline_sentence": "Under equal weight per benchmark cell (8 cells, 1/8 each), the accuracy-max setting beats always-32B-direct on accuracy by +0.0019 [-0.0012, +0.0047] -- but it now costs 1.75x that baseline's compute, not less, and the compute-lean setting neither matches it on the multiple-choice half (-0.0070 [-0.0126, -0.0017], a SIGNIFICANT LOSS) nor stays cheap (1.48x compute, up from 0.49x sample-weighted); the one baseline the method still clearly beats at equal weight is a 32B actually made to reason (+0.0611 [+0.0510, +0.0709] accuracy, -88% latency, -84% energy -- though not fewer FLOP-eq: 1.75x as charged, 1.41x honestly re-costed)."
